  "id": "emicetic-distinction",
  "term": "emic–etic distinction",
  "definition": "The emic–etic distinction is a way of understanding behaviour or experience from two standpoints: an insider view and an outsider view. In this usage, emic refers to people’s own account of their experiences, while etic refers to how another person or observer describes those experiences or behaviour.",
